    {
      "sectionId": "section-duergar-traits",
      "heading": "Duergar Traits",
      "sourceAnchor": "duergar-traits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-duergar-traits-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section reflects the traits published in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Monsters of the Multiverse",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/motm/fantastical-races#Duergar"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-duergar-traits-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ability Score Increases"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": The standardized choice of +2/+1 or three +1’s that because common after the release of Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "text": "Age"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Rarely impactful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Size"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Medium is very slightly better than\n\t\tSmall because you can’t be grappled or swallowed whole by as many\n\t\tenemies."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Speed"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Standard."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Darkvision"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Darkvision is already great,\nbut getting twice as much as range as everyone else is a massive advantage in large, unlit areas."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Duergar Magic"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Both decent buffs, especially for martial characters. It’s not clear if you can use spell slots to cast them on other creatures, unfortunately. Check with your DM. The community leans towards allowing you to target other creatures when you use a spell slot."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Dwarven Resilience"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Resistance to the most common non-weapon damage type in the game."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Psionic Fortitude"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Only situationally useful, but still a nice defense."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Languages"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Common+1 is standard."
              }
            ]
          ],
